WEBVTT

00:00:01.490 --> 00:00:04.130
You want to meet Ultra-rare?

00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:04.770
Yes!

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:09.970
I heard that Ultra-rare beat you 
in a Vanguard fight, Brother Aichi!

00:00:09.970 --> 00:00:14.930
If I were to fight them, it'll strengthen 
my skills for the nationals!

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:19.700
Drop by the shop again sometime.

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:25.220
Sure, let's go.

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:30.430
All right! With that decided, 
gather up, Team Q4!

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:34.170
I have no interest in a card shop like that.

00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:36.100
Hey, Kai!

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:37.200
Kai?

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.260
See you guys!

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:43.260
What's <i>his</i> problem?!

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:44.550
Let's forget about him!

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:49.270
I'm not going.

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:54.490
Don't you have any aspirin or aspersions?!

00:00:55.490 --> 00:00:56.670
Asp...

00:00:56.670 --> 00:00:57.710
Asp...?

00:00:58.070 --> 00:00:59.520
Maybe "aspirations"?

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:02.430
Y-Yeah! That's it!

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:03.780
Aspirations!

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:05.280
I forgot them in my room.

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:09.480
Don't say that. How about going with them?

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:11.380
Who's going to help you with the store?

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:15.850
Consider it a part of the job.

00:01:16.410 --> 00:01:19.020
Please check out the rival shop.

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:20.770
See you later!

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:26.430
Whoo! Ultra-rare! I can't 
wait, Brother Aichi!

00:01:26.430 --> 00:01:27.100
Yep.

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:30.590
I heard.

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:33.280
You're going to meet my Kourin?

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:35.450
<i>Fine!</i>

00:01:35.450 --> 00:01:38.630
As a representative member 
of the Ultra-rare Fan Club...

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:42.080
I'll bring you guys there!

00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:48.770
This guy <i>always</i> shows up when he isn't 
needed and tries to tag along...

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:26.390
Huh? Where was it again?

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:28.840
Some guide you are...

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:31.640
Oh, shut up! I'll find it, I'll find it!

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:36.180
As long as I have my love for Kourin, 
I'll always be able to find her!

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:39.020
Kourin, wait for me!

00:03:39.020 --> 00:03:41.240
He's a serious case, in more ways than one.

00:03:41.470 --> 00:03:44.730
Brother Aichi, don't you 
remember where it is?

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:48.610
I'm trying to recall, but...

00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:55.870
Whoa.

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:02.290
Ultra-rare's in there...

00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:04.690
Card Shop PSY...

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:08.530
Hey, everyone!

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:11.060
Aichi!

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:13.010
So this is where it was!

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:14.570
I thought so.

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:16.670
Huh?

00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:17.430
What the...?!

00:04:19.110 --> 00:04:22.580
Hey! Guys! Open the door!

00:04:22.580 --> 00:04:24.130
Let me meet Kourin!

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:25.470
Let me meet her!

00:04:27.020 --> 00:04:30.460
Shouldn't we wait for Morikawa?

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:31.860
Nah.

00:04:31.860 --> 00:04:34.620
Exactly! He's not a little kid.

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:36.660
More importantly, this is...

00:04:38.690 --> 00:04:42.350
Wow! They've got rare cards on display!

00:04:42.350 --> 00:04:44.410
It looks like no one's around...

00:04:45.700 --> 00:04:46.850
Over there...

00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:50.600
Um...

00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:53.140
H-Hello.

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:06.090
Fateful Encounter

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:09.340
Uh, who are you...?

00:05:11.480 --> 00:05:12.420
I am...

00:05:16.590 --> 00:05:18.080
not an employee here.

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:22.770
Th-That wasn't what I meant...

00:05:22.770 --> 00:05:25.170
Oh. I'm not a customer either.

00:05:26.380 --> 00:05:29.390
Got it! So, where's Ultra-rare?

00:05:29.390 --> 00:05:31.130
Nor am I a member of Ultra-rare.

00:05:32.780 --> 00:05:34.760
What's with this guy?

00:05:34.760 --> 00:05:36.580
I-I don't know...

00:05:36.580 --> 00:05:39.020
Welcome to Card Shop PSY.

00:05:40.050 --> 00:05:42.090
W-When did <i>you</i> get here?!

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:45.570
What's <i>he</i> doing here?!

00:05:45.770 --> 00:05:47.710
I invited him.

00:05:47.710 --> 00:05:50.420
But the three of us decided...

00:05:50.420 --> 00:05:52.480
I appreciate both of you coming...

00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:55.540
Aichi Sendou...

00:05:56.600 --> 00:05:57.670
and...

00:05:57.670 --> 00:05:59.370
Ren Suzugamori.

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:01.350
Ren Suzugamori?!

00:06:01.350 --> 00:06:04.010
You don't mean <i>that</i> Ren Suzugamori?!

00:06:04.010 --> 00:06:07.870
That's right! In the last Vanguard 
Fight National Championship...

00:06:07.870 --> 00:06:11.360
his team participated for the first time, 
but won through overwhelming strength!

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:13.600
He's the leader of Team Foo Fighter!

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:15.960
I've heard his name before...

00:06:15.960 --> 00:06:18.850
but didn't expect he'd be an 
absent-minded guy like <i>this</i>!

00:06:18.850 --> 00:06:20.500
The national champion...

00:06:21.090 --> 00:06:22.530
<i>Really?</i>

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:26.020
Let's get down to business, Ren Suzugamori.

00:06:26.020 --> 00:06:29.650
As agreed, you'll show us your 
prowess at Vanguard fighting.

00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:32.700
A Vanguard fight...

00:06:34.570 --> 00:06:36.550
He seems different...

00:06:36.550 --> 00:06:38.890
You want to fight me, yes?

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:39.620
Indeed.

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:46.090
Sure. You three are qualified.

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:49.470
We're lucky! Who'd ever guess 
we'd be able to get a sneak peek

00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:52.370
at the national champ's ability 
in a place like this?!

00:06:52.370 --> 00:06:53.610
Y-Yeah...

00:06:55.610 --> 00:06:57.400
You'll use this deck.

00:06:58.150 --> 00:06:58.990
Thanks.

00:07:04.170 --> 00:07:06.860
A deck of mostly female units?

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:09.800
Certainly, this would put a 
player's ability to the test.

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:18.830
Where am I?!

00:07:34.240 --> 00:07:35.860
What... was that just now?

00:07:39.490 --> 00:07:41.640
It looks like you'll become the trump card...

00:07:45.590 --> 00:07:47.280
...looks like we were not mistaken.

00:07:47.280 --> 00:07:48.060
Right.

00:07:48.060 --> 00:07:48.820
Yes.

00:07:49.310 --> 00:07:51.320
I'm ready when you are.

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:52.590
This way.

00:07:52.590 --> 00:07:53.830
You three, as well...

00:07:53.830 --> 00:07:56.250
I'm sure this is going to 
be an interesting fight.

00:07:56.250 --> 00:07:57.130
Yesss!

00:07:57.130 --> 00:07:59.040
Th-Thank you.

00:08:02.830 --> 00:08:05.680
My deck is exactly the same as yours.

00:08:05.680 --> 00:08:09.920
In other words, we'll be able to clearly see 
the difference between our abilities, right?

00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:16.600
I'm so excited! What kind 
of fight is this gonna be?!

00:08:16.600 --> 00:08:18.830
A fight with the national champion...

00:08:24.120 --> 00:08:26.450
You know what I like about Vanguard fights?

00:08:26.450 --> 00:08:32.860
You don't harm your opponent, you don't need 
courage, and you can just keep winning.

00:08:33.970 --> 00:08:35.070
Let's begin.

00:08:40.990 --> 00:08:43.830
Stand up the Vanguard!

00:08:40.990 --> 00:08:43.830
Stand up, Vanguard!

00:08:45.960 --> 00:08:47.420
I'm up first.

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:48.560
Draw!

00:08:48.560 --> 00:08:50.570
I ride Battle Sister, Chocolat!

00:08:53.360 --> 00:08:56.050
Sphere Magus uses her skill to 
move to a rear-guard circle!

00:08:59.020 --> 00:09:00.260
That's the end of my turn.

00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:02.320
Ren Suzugamori...

00:09:02.740 --> 00:09:04.600
I wonder how he'll fight...

00:09:05.120 --> 00:09:07.510
I ride Weather Girl, Milk.

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:12.170
Sphere Magus moves to a Rear-guard circle.

00:09:12.170 --> 00:09:14.200
I call Battle Sister, Cocoa.

00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:20.370
With Cocoa's skill, I check 
the top card of my deck...

00:09:20.980 --> 00:09:22.620
and leave it on top.

00:09:23.130 --> 00:09:25.080
I attack Chocolat with Milk!

00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:30.210
Drive trigger check.

00:09:32.230 --> 00:09:34.050
Damage trigger check.

00:09:34.930 --> 00:09:36.300
I attack with Cocoa.

00:09:41.950 --> 00:09:43.770
Damage trigger check.

00:09:44.650 --> 00:09:45.870
That's the end of my turn.

00:09:45.870 --> 00:09:47.980
I stand and draw.

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:51.390
I ride Top Idol Aqua.

00:09:58.140 --> 00:10:00.470
I call Blazer Pleasures and Milk.

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:07.990
I use the Pleasures' skill 
to add +2000 power to Aqua.

00:10:10.200 --> 00:10:12.200
I call one more Pleasures.

00:10:13.950 --> 00:10:17.310
With their skill, I give +2000 
power to the Pleasures on the left.

00:10:18.580 --> 00:10:20.930
The Pleasures attack your Vanguard!

00:10:29.510 --> 00:10:31.280
Damage trigger check.

00:10:32.390 --> 00:10:34.750
I attack with Aqua, boosted by Milk!

00:10:41.640 --> 00:10:43.300
Drive trigger check.

00:10:48.560 --> 00:10:50.580
Damage trigger check.

00:10:50.870 --> 00:10:53.670
I attack with the other Pleasures, 
boosted by Sphere Magus!

00:10:54.230 --> 00:10:56.730
But first, I use Sphere's skill 
to give them +3000 power!

00:11:04.340 --> 00:11:06.230
Damage trigger check.

00:11:08.420 --> 00:11:11.410
After boosting, Sphere 
Magus returns to the deck.

00:11:12.440 --> 00:11:15.350
Wow. That's already 3 damage!

00:11:15.350 --> 00:11:18.360
The way she's fighting takes 
advantage of going first.

00:11:18.360 --> 00:11:22.630
See, she can call high-grade 
units before her opponent.

00:11:22.630 --> 00:11:26.140
Naturally, if the grade is 
high, its power is also high.

00:11:26.140 --> 00:11:31.730
So even without a unit to give a boost from the 
rear, it's possible to hit home with three attacks.

00:11:31.730 --> 00:11:37.290
So does that negate the advantage of taking 
the field first and being able to attack first?

00:11:37.290 --> 00:11:40.260
Well, what's the national champ gonna do?

00:11:45.900 --> 00:11:47.950
What is this feeling...?

00:11:59.580 --> 00:12:01.290
It's your turn.

00:12:01.290 --> 00:12:04.000
Right. Stand and draw.

00:12:05.100 --> 00:12:07.040
I ride Maiden of Libra.

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:14.070
I move Cocoa back and call Lady Bomb.

00:12:15.950 --> 00:12:18.620
Libra, boosted by Sphere Magus...

00:12:18.620 --> 00:12:20.340
attacks the Pleasures!

00:12:21.360 --> 00:12:23.680
Not the Vanguard, but the rear-guard?!

00:12:23.680 --> 00:12:26.810
I use Sphere's skill to 
add +3000 power to Libra.

00:12:30.680 --> 00:12:32.560
Drive trigger check.

00:12:36.050 --> 00:12:37.690
Counterblast.

00:12:38.060 --> 00:12:42.610
When Libra makes a successful attack, 
one card can be drawn from the deck.

00:12:45.280 --> 00:12:46.970
Cocoa boosts.

00:12:46.970 --> 00:12:49.620
Lady Bomb attacks your other Pleasures!

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:51.990
Another attack on the rear-guard?!

00:12:52.250 --> 00:12:55.730
I guard with Bermuda Triangle Cadet Caravel!

00:12:59.380 --> 00:13:01.300
Sphere returns to the deck.

00:13:01.880 --> 00:13:09.050
I see! To erase her advantage of getting to 
draw first, the champ targeted her rear-guard!

00:13:09.920 --> 00:13:12.850
She lined up her grade 1 units in the front,

00:13:12.850 --> 00:13:15.830
and he exploited the gap in 
the line after she attacked.

00:13:15.830 --> 00:13:19.860
They're both erasing each other's 
advantage of going first or second...

00:13:19.860 --> 00:13:21.280
This is an incredible fight!

00:13:21.570 --> 00:13:23.710
Kourin has two cards in her hand.

00:13:24.020 --> 00:13:25.450
Ren has six cards.

00:13:25.450 --> 00:13:27.690
That's some gap!

00:13:27.690 --> 00:13:32.320
He made Kourin use the cards in her hand and 
increased his cards with that Counterblast.

00:13:32.320 --> 00:13:34.500
Even though it's the first 
time he's using that deck...

00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:38.410
Of course, we'd be in trouble if 
he weren't at least this good.

00:13:39.320 --> 00:13:41.420
I stand and draw!

00:13:43.060 --> 00:13:45.340
I ride Top Idol Flores!

00:13:48.920 --> 00:13:52.080
I move Pleasures back and call Cadet Caravel!

00:13:54.840 --> 00:13:56.590
Caravel's Soulblast!

00:13:58.020 --> 00:13:59.980
Kourin's hand increased too!

00:14:00.240 --> 00:14:03.600
I attack your Vanguard with 
Flores, boosted by Milk!

00:14:07.820 --> 00:14:09.810
Twin drive first check...

00:14:10.530 --> 00:14:11.880
Second check...

00:14:14.320 --> 00:14:16.950
I attack with Caravel, boosted by Pleasures!

00:14:18.800 --> 00:14:20.080
I guard with Aqua.

00:14:24.570 --> 00:14:25.890
That's the end of my turn.

00:14:28.300 --> 00:14:30.550
The fight's only just begun!

00:14:30.820 --> 00:14:31.770
Draw.

00:14:32.340 --> 00:14:33.930
I ride Flores.

00:14:39.820 --> 00:14:41.860
And then I call another Flores.

00:14:48.290 --> 00:14:50.070
I call Pleasures.

00:14:50.070 --> 00:14:53.800
What, a grade 1?! What a tease!

00:14:53.800 --> 00:14:56.280
You sound like Morikawa.

00:14:57.790 --> 00:15:00.740
That has the same skill 
as my Starlight Unicorn...

00:15:03.190 --> 00:15:05.420
It looks like you'll become the trump card...

00:15:06.540 --> 00:15:08.300
<i>That's</i> the trump card?

00:15:09.270 --> 00:15:14.010
I use the Pleasures' skill to add +2000 
to the power of my Vanguard, Flores.

00:15:14.610 --> 00:15:17.390
I attack your Vanguard 
with my rear-guard Flores.

00:15:21.810 --> 00:15:26.010
I attack your Vanguard with 
Flores, boosted by the Pleasures.

00:15:29.280 --> 00:15:30.780
Twin drive.

00:15:30.780 --> 00:15:32.250
First check...

00:15:33.460 --> 00:15:34.860
Second check...

00:15:35.710 --> 00:15:39.460
Draw trigger. I add +5000 
to the power of Lady Bomb.

00:15:40.090 --> 00:15:41.460
And then I draw.

00:15:43.170 --> 00:15:45.170
Damage trigger check.

00:15:46.840 --> 00:15:48.490
Critical trigger!

00:15:48.490 --> 00:15:50.580
I give +5000 to the power of Flores,

00:15:50.580 --> 00:15:52.180
and give her the critical +1.

00:15:52.400 --> 00:15:53.780
Soulblast.

00:15:54.380 --> 00:16:00.960
When Flores makes a successful attack, a 
Bermuda Triangle unit can be returned to the hand.

00:16:00.960 --> 00:16:02.190
I return...

00:16:02.580 --> 00:16:04.400
Blazer Pleasures!

00:16:04.400 --> 00:16:06.800
His hand's increasing again!

00:16:06.800 --> 00:16:08.900
Is this really his first time with that deck?

00:16:09.990 --> 00:16:13.160
How can he use it this well? 
I'm sure we're all curious.

00:16:13.160 --> 00:16:15.620
Lady Bomb is boosted by Cocoa...

00:16:15.620 --> 00:16:17.320
and attacks your Vanguard!

00:16:18.280 --> 00:16:20.370
I guard with Sphere Magus!

00:16:26.800 --> 00:16:28.090
That's the end of my turn.

00:16:28.750 --> 00:16:30.950
They both have 4 damage!

00:16:30.950 --> 00:16:33.180
Here's where Kourin clinches it!

00:16:33.180 --> 00:16:33.800
Mm-hm.

00:16:38.540 --> 00:16:42.190
I retire Cadet Caravel and call Flores!

00:16:45.470 --> 00:16:47.230
I call Aqua and Chocolat!

00:16:53.870 --> 00:16:56.070
I like that look in your eyes...

00:16:56.560 --> 00:16:59.620
Unfortunately, though, you 
won't be able to beat me.

00:17:04.240 --> 00:17:06.060
You'll have to prove it.

00:17:06.060 --> 00:17:08.460
I attack with Aqua, boosted by Chocolat!

00:17:11.250 --> 00:17:13.470
I guard with Cadet Caravel!

00:17:15.630 --> 00:17:18.330
I attack with Flores, boosted by Milk!

00:17:19.660 --> 00:17:23.140
I guard with Oracle Guardian, 
Nike and Sphere Magus.

00:17:25.140 --> 00:17:27.460
Twin drive first check...

00:17:27.460 --> 00:17:29.050
Second check...

00:17:30.480 --> 00:17:32.090
Critical trigger!

00:17:32.090 --> 00:17:36.610
I give the Flores who hasn't attacked 
yet the +5000 power <i>and</i> the critical +1!

00:17:40.130 --> 00:17:42.890
I attack with Flores, 
boosted by the Pleasures!

00:17:47.190 --> 00:17:50.480
I guard with Lady Bomb, 
Dream Eater, and Libra!

00:17:55.300 --> 00:17:57.570
Wow! Three guards!

00:17:57.570 --> 00:17:59.010
My turn's over...

00:17:59.330 --> 00:18:03.220
Even with the critical trigger, 
he didn't take any damage...

00:18:03.790 --> 00:18:06.590
See? Just like I said.

00:18:06.590 --> 00:18:08.510
I can see it...

00:18:08.510 --> 00:18:09.930
Everything.

00:18:16.590 --> 00:18:17.610
There we go.

00:18:42.190 --> 00:18:45.070
Again... What's happening to me?!

00:18:46.980 --> 00:18:48.360
Final turn.

00:18:51.420 --> 00:18:52.900
I call Pleasures!

00:18:55.100 --> 00:18:58.530
I use their skill to add +2000 to 
the power of my rear-guard Flores.

00:18:59.290 --> 00:19:03.460
And then I use the skill of my other 
Pleasures to add another +2000 to the same Flores.

00:19:04.490 --> 00:19:05.580
Oh, no...

00:19:05.580 --> 00:19:08.000
It seems like you've caught on.

00:19:10.230 --> 00:19:14.450
I attack your Vanguard with my 
Lady Bomb, boosted by Cocoa.

00:19:15.510 --> 00:19:16.460
No guard.

00:19:20.510 --> 00:19:22.470
Damage trigger check!

00:19:22.920 --> 00:19:25.720
No heal trigger...?

00:19:27.980 --> 00:19:30.610
Flores is boosted by Pleasures...

00:19:30.610 --> 00:19:32.350
and attacks your Vanguard.

00:19:32.350 --> 00:19:33.440
I guard with Nike!

00:19:36.190 --> 00:19:37.900
Twin drive.

00:19:37.900 --> 00:19:39.010
First check...

00:19:39.470 --> 00:19:41.020
Second check...

00:19:49.330 --> 00:19:52.210
She managed to protect herself, 
but that still leaves...

00:19:52.440 --> 00:19:54.790
Flores, with +4000 power...

00:19:55.330 --> 00:19:59.130
I attack with Flores, 
boosted by the Pleasures!

00:20:02.130 --> 00:20:06.050
Intercept with Aqua, making 
the shield +5000...

00:20:06.050 --> 00:20:07.920
After that, it's up to 
what she has in her hand.

00:20:11.840 --> 00:20:13.000
No guard.

00:20:14.500 --> 00:20:16.350
Take that!

00:20:19.060 --> 00:20:20.920
Damage trigger check.

00:20:26.490 --> 00:20:28.010
I lose.

00:20:31.140 --> 00:20:34.110
His last attack was 20000 power.

00:20:34.110 --> 00:20:37.570
Even if she'd used Aqua and Cocoa, 
her shield would've been 20000.

00:20:37.570 --> 00:20:39.710
He hit her with an exact attack.

00:20:40.870 --> 00:20:42.970
The key to this fight...

00:20:42.970 --> 00:20:44.320
was those two cards.

00:20:45.380 --> 00:20:50.310
Blazer Pleasures, with only +2000 power, 
determined the outcome of the fight.

00:20:54.340 --> 00:20:55.870
Could that have been...

00:20:56.350 --> 00:20:58.450
a hint that this would happen?

00:20:58.780 --> 00:20:59.860
Impossible...

00:21:01.160 --> 00:21:03.740
What is this?! Suddenly, 
my head feels so heavy...

00:21:03.740 --> 00:21:05.170
Brother Aichi...

00:21:05.170 --> 00:21:06.150
Are you okay?

00:21:06.150 --> 00:21:07.600
Y-Yeah...

00:21:11.480 --> 00:21:13.910
You're a decent fighter.

00:21:13.910 --> 00:21:16.640
But you're no match for me.

00:21:17.240 --> 00:21:18.540
Not by a long shot.

00:21:19.780 --> 00:21:22.170
It turned out the way we expected.

00:21:22.750 --> 00:21:23.750
You have...

00:21:23.750 --> 00:21:25.300
You can feel my power, can't you?

00:21:26.380 --> 00:21:28.060
What's your motive?

00:21:28.060 --> 00:21:32.010
Well, we'll decide whether or not to talk 
about that after watching the next tournament.

00:21:32.280 --> 00:21:33.450
Is that so?

00:21:34.090 --> 00:21:37.010
Then you can watch me at the next tournament.

00:21:37.010 --> 00:21:40.570
There's something I'd like to 
discuss with the three of you then.

00:21:40.570 --> 00:21:41.900
About power...

00:21:47.430 --> 00:21:49.840
I will not acknowledge a guy like that.

00:21:49.840 --> 00:21:52.510
But the fact is, he's 
currently the top fighter.

00:21:52.510 --> 00:21:54.400
He's good-looking, so I don't see a problem!

00:21:54.400 --> 00:21:56.170
It's not about his looks!

00:21:56.170 --> 00:21:57.390
Yeah, yeah!

00:21:57.390 --> 00:21:58.890
Anyway...

00:21:58.890 --> 00:22:01.220
it wasn't necessary to invite 
that boy over, was it?

00:22:01.980 --> 00:22:03.800
He's fine as he is.

00:22:07.960 --> 00:22:11.150
Ask, and the exit shall be open unto you...

00:22:16.470 --> 00:22:17.920
Who's that?

00:23:51.400 --> 00:23:54.490
Ren Suzugamori isn't the 
national champ for nothing!

00:23:54.490 --> 00:23:58.030
Amazing! I fought Kourin once, 
and a player as strong as her...

00:23:58.030 --> 00:23:59.800
It just goes to show how strong he is.

00:23:59.800 --> 00:24:02.700
The national championship is 
gonna be full of guys like that.

00:24:02.700 --> 00:24:04.940
Misaki's power of memory...

00:24:04.940 --> 00:24:07.170
Maybe it'll become a great asset!

00:24:07.170 --> 00:24:10.010
Yeah! She said she remembered the rules 
after looking at them only once...

00:24:10.010 --> 00:24:13.170
And if she can remember the abilities and 
triggers of the units that are in her hand,

00:24:13.170 --> 00:24:15.170
thats a great advantage, you know?!

00:24:15.170 --> 00:24:17.180
Next time: The Indelible Memory!

00:24:17.510 --> 00:24:18.280
Misaki...
